{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3063","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3063","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3063\",\"parent_revision\":\"565f6ceaf9bca14f5230532cd454b2362f3cb7c1\",\"root_revision\":\"6a0efc6fc9ddf9a464d0d959a33bd75f70b50e25a576cba46ec0968e84c4178c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe CLI does not accept the address, map, or page-window parameters. Ordinal navigation is unreachable from the CLI entirely, while the same operations expose it through the MCP transport.\\n\\nThe contract binds behaviour to every transport. A capability present on one transport and absent on the other is a gap, not a design.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] The CLI accepts the same address, map, and page parameters as the other transport\\n- [ ] Identical inputs produce identical logical results on both transports\\n- [ ] A capability added to one transport is added to the shared operations layer, not to a transport module\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- Intended behaviour is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/agent-markdown-consumption-contract.md`. Component ownership is defined in `plugins/development-harness/docs/component-architecture.md`. Parent: #3054.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"3db1ae58fe64b7e8dbee54527b17410b75ef9d5046d50b30d254396713853392\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABXPQ6dg\"}"}